---
import LegalPage from "../components/LegalPage.astro";

const sections = [
  ["introduction", "Introduction"],
  ["reporting", "Reporting security issues"],
  ["safe-harbor", "Responsible research and safe harbor"],
  ["practices", "Our security practices"],
  ["responsibilities", "Your responsibilities"],
  ["scope", "Scope"],
  ["updates", "Updates to this policy"],
  ["contact", "Contact us"],
] as const;
---

<LegalPage
  title="Security Policy — Modesto"
  description="How to report security issues in Modesto and how the project approaches product security."
  heading="Modesto Security Policy"
  lede="Security is a shared responsibility. This policy explains how to report a vulnerability, how we protect the software and channels we operate, and how you can secure the environments and providers you connect to Modesto."
  effectiveDate="2026-09-08"
  lastUpdated="2026-09-08"
  sections={sections}
>
  <section id="introduction">
    <p class="section-number">01</p>
    <h2>Introduction</h2>
    <p>
      This Security Policy describes the vulnerability-reporting process and security practices for
      the Modesto desktop application, the website at{" "}<a href="https://modesto.dev"
        >https://modesto.dev</a
      >, and release artifacts published at{" "}<a href="https://github.com/Syphon1205/Modesto"
        >https://github.com/Syphon1205/Modesto</a
      >.
    </p>
    <p>
      Modesto is local-first. It connects software running on your devices with coding-agent
      harnesses and providers you choose. We secure the application we ship, the Site we operate,
      and the GitHub release channel we publish. We do not control the security of your devices,
      environments, repositories, networks, credentials, or third-party providers. Please review
      the shared responsibilities below when assessing risk.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section id="reporting">
    <p class="section-number">02</p>
    <h2>Reporting Security Issues</h2>
    <p>
      If you believe you have found a security vulnerability affecting Modesto, report it
      privately. Do not open a public GitHub issue for an unpatched security report.
    </p>
    <p>Preferred path:</p>
    <ol>
      <li>
        Open a private GitHub Security Advisory at{" "}<a
          href="https://github.com/Syphon1205/Modesto/security/advisories/new"
          >github.com/Syphon1205/Modesto/security/advisories/new</a
        >.
      </li>
      <li>
        Include enough detail to reproduce the issue, the affected version or commit, and any
        known workaround.
      </li>
      <li>Allow a reasonable time for triage before any public disclosure.</li>
    </ol>
    <p>Please include, when available:</p>
    <ul>
      <li>A description of the issue and its potential impact;</li>
      <li>The affected application, version, URL, endpoint, or component;</li>
      <li>Clear reproduction steps or a minimal proof of concept;</li>
      <li>Relevant logs, screenshots, or request and response details with secrets removed; and</li>
      <li>Your preferred contact information and whether you want public credit.</li>
    </ul>
    <p>
      You can also contact the maintainer privately via GitHub:{" "}<a
        href="https://github.com/Syphon1205">@Syphon1205</a
      >. We aim to acknowledge complete reports as soon as practical, confirm the issue, assess
      impact, and work on a fix for the latest supported release when appropriate. Resolution time
      varies with severity, complexity, and dependencies on third parties. Credit will be given to
      reporters who want it, unless they prefer to remain anonymous.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section id="safe-harbor">
    <p class="section-number">03</p>
    <h2>Responsible Research and Safe Harbor</h2>
    <p>
      We support good-faith security research. If you make a genuine effort to comply with this
      policy, avoid harm, respect privacy, and report findings promptly, we will treat your
      research as authorized and will not initiate legal action against you for accidental,
      good-faith violations of this policy. If a third party initiates legal action concerning
      compliant research, we will make our authorization known where appropriate.
    </p>
    <p>To remain within this safe harbor, you must:</p>
    <ul>
      <li>Test only accounts, data, and systems you own or have explicit permission to test;</li>
      <li>Stop and report immediately if you encounter personal, confidential, or production data;</li>
      <li>Access only the minimum information needed to demonstrate the issue;</li>
      <li>Avoid disrupting availability, degrading performance, or damaging or deleting data;</li>
      <li>Not use social engineering, phishing, physical attacks, or denial-of-service testing;</li>
      <li>Not test third-party services or infrastructure outside Modesto’s control; and</li>
      <li>Give us reasonable time to address the issue before public disclosure.</li>
    </ul>
    <p>
      This safe harbor does not authorize violations of law or activity outside the scope of this
      policy. Vulnerability rewards are not guaranteed and, if offered, are determined by the
      project in its discretion.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section id="practices">
    <p class="section-number">04</p>
    <h2>Our Security Practices</h2>
    <p>
      We use administrative, technical, and organizational safeguards designed for a local-first
      desktop product and a public website. These practices include:
    </p>
    <ul>
      <li>
        <strong>Data minimization.</strong> Modesto is designed so coding-session content can
        remain between your clients, your environment, and the harnesses and providers you
        configure. We do not operate a cloud session broker that archives your prompts or source
        while an agent is working.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Encrypted transport.</strong> The Site and GitHub-hosted update metadata use
        encrypted transport. Connections from the App to providers you configure use those
        providers’ own transport and authentication.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Credential protection.</strong> The App uses platform-provided protected storage
        for credentials and session tokens where supported. We design logging so secrets are not
        collected unless you voluntarily attach them to a report.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Signed desktop builds.</strong> Published macOS builds are Developer ID signed and
        notarized by Apple. Release artifacts and updater manifests are published from the
        project’s GitHub release channel.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Supported versions.</strong> Security fixes are prioritized for the latest stable
        desktop release published on the{" "}<a href="https://github.com/Syphon1205/Modesto/releases"
          >Modesto releases page</a
        >. Older releases receive best-effort attention.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Maintenance.</strong> We review dependencies, ship updates, and publish
        mitigations as appropriate. The App’s built-in updater is the intended path for receiving
        those fixes.
      </li>
    </ul>
    <p>
      No system is completely secure. These practices reduce risk but do not guarantee that the
      Site or Services will be free from vulnerabilities or unauthorized access.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section id="responsibilities">
    <p class="section-number">05</p>
    <h2>Your Responsibilities</h2>
    <p>
      Because you control much of the Modesto execution path, you play an important role in
      securing it. You are responsible for:
    </p>
    <ul>
      <li>Keeping Modesto, your operating systems, and connected tools up to date;</li>
      <li>Securing your devices, repositories, environments, networks, and backups;</li>
      <li>Protecting account, provider, repository, and environment credentials;</li>
      <li>Using multi-factor authentication where your identity and coding-agent providers support it;</li>
      <li>Granting providers and integrations only the permissions they need;</li>
      <li>Reviewing commands, source changes, and other agent output before applying or executing it;</li>
      <li>Removing lost or unused devices and revoking credentials you believe may be compromised; and</li>
      <li>Following the security policies of your selected harnesses, providers, and infrastructure.</li>
    </ul>
    <p>
      Do not send passwords, API keys, access tokens, or private keys in a vulnerability report.
      Revoke any secret that may have been exposed before sharing sanitized evidence with us.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section id="scope">
    <p class="section-number">06</p>
    <h2>Scope</h2>
    <p>In-scope examples include:</p>
    <ul>
      <li>Remote code execution or sandbox escapes in the desktop app or update path;</li>
      <li>Credential, token, or secret leakage through Modesto surfaces;</li>
      <li>Privilege escalation or unauthorized access to local project or session data; and</li>
      <li>Supply-chain issues in published Modesto release artifacts.</li>
    </ul>
    <p>Out-of-scope examples include:</p>
    <ul>
      <li>
        Vulnerabilities only in third-party agent providers (Codex, Claude, Cursor, and similar)
        that Modesto does not control;
      </li>
      <li>Issues that require an already-compromised local machine with full user access; and</li>
      <li>Social-engineering reports without a technical vulnerability.</li>
    </ul>
  </section>

  <section id="updates">
    <p class="section-number">07</p>
    <h2>Updates to This Policy</h2>
    <p>
      We may update this Security Policy as Modesto, our infrastructure, and security practices
      evolve. We will post revisions at this URL and update the dates above. Material changes to
      the vulnerability-reporting process or safe-harbor terms will apply prospectively.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section id="contact">
    <p class="section-number">08</p>
    <h2>Contact Us</h2>
    <p>
      Report security issues through a{" "}<a
        href="https://github.com/Syphon1205/Modesto/security/advisories/new"
        >private GitHub Security Advisory</a
      >.
    </p>
    <p>
      For general questions about the project, use the public repository at{" "}<a
        href="https://github.com/Syphon1205/Modesto">github.com/Syphon1205/Modesto</a
      >. For privacy requests, see the{" "}<a href="/privacy-policy">Privacy Policy</a>.
    </p>
  </section>
</LegalPage>
